# lane/lowbit-mma-speed: time and rate per arm

Written by `tools/lowbit_mma_speed/table.py --levers`. `over` is the arm's median
over fp32.v1's at the same shape on the same box; above 1 the arm took longer.
One run per box; the median of the timed calls, the minimum beside it.
An arm named `probe.*` computes a WRONG product on purpose (a part of a kernel,
timed alone): it has no identity and is no plan.

